<p>Kenya’s National Intelligence Service has told lawmakers that more than 1,000 Kenyans were recruited to fight for Russia in Ukraine—far higher than earlier estimates—bringing sharper scrutiny in Nairobi. Several reports say recruits were drawn in through false or misleading job offers linked to Russia, only to end up tied to the Russian military effort in Ukraine. Russia’s embassy in Nairobi has denied that Moscow is illegally recruiting Kenyans, while saying foreign citizens can voluntarily join Russia’s armed forces. Russia has also blamed Kenya for stalled labor-migration and security-cooperation talks linked to the dispute, highlighting the wider strain on relations.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Parliamentary scrutiny: The National Intelligence Service briefed lawmakers this week, moving the issue into formal parliamentary oversight.</li><li>Scale vs prior estimates: The agency’s figure is about five times higher than earlier estimates cited by authorities.</li><li>Arrests reported: Kenyan authorities have arrested suspected recruiters, according to coverage, as scrutiny grows.</li><li>Embassy denial: Russia’s embassy in Nairobi rejected claims of illegal recruitment, but said foreigners may join Russia’s military voluntarily.</li><li>Family demands: Families have appealed for help to bring relatives home after learning they were recruited into Russia’s army and sent toward the conflict zone.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Kenya’s National Intelligence Service: The agency told lawmakers that more than 1,000 Kenyans were recruited to fight for Russia in Ukraine—well above earlier estimates cited by officials. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3344104/over-1000-kenyans-recruited-fight-russia-ukraine-war-report'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Kenyan families: Relatives of those recruited have publicly asked authorities for help bringing loved ones home after learning they were pulled into Russia’s war effort. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/19/kenyan-families-demand-return-of-loved-ones-conscripted-by-russian-army'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Russian officials (as reported by Kenyan media): Russia blamed Kenya for stalled labor-migration and security-cooperation talks tied to the dispute, arguing the row is hurting wider bilateral engagement. (<a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202602190605.html'>AllAfrica (Capital FM)</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/a-thousand-kenyans-recruited-for-russia-s-war-new-report/a-76050872'>A thousand Kenyans &#x27;recruited&#x27; for Russia&#x27;s war — new report</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3344104/over-1000-kenyans-recruited-fight-russia-ukraine-war-report'>Over 1,000 Kenyans recruited to fight for Russia in Ukraine war: report</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/19/kenyan-families-demand-return-of-loved-ones-conscripted-by-russian-army'>Kenyan families demand return of loved ones recruited into Russian army</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202602190605.html'>Kenya: Russia Claims Stalled Labour, Security Talks With Kenya Amid Recruitment Row</a> - allafrica.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/over-1000-kenyans-recruited-to-fight-for-russia-in-ukraine-report-says'>Over 1,000 Kenyans recruited to fight for Russia in Ukraine, report says</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/kenyan-report-alleges-1000-citizens-recruited-to-fight-for-russia-in-ukraine-13981763.html'>Kenyan report alleges 1,000 citizens recruited to fight for Russia in Ukraine</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/02/19/g-s1-110724/russia-ukraine-war-kenyans-recruited'>1,000 Kenyans were recruited to fight for Russia in Ukraine, intelligence report says</a> - npr.org</li></ul>